    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1935705392052380128",
      "url": "https://x.com/enterdonatello/status/1935705392052380128",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/enterdonatello/status/1935705392052380128",
      "text": "Unfortunately, no exchange is completely immune from such incidents.\n\nAs for the threat to individuals  I completely agree.\nHere’s a quick recap of recent events:\n\n🇫🇷 Ledger Founder and Wife Kidnapped, Later Freed\n\nOn January 21, David Balland founder of the Ledger crypto wallet and his wife Amandine Balland were kidnapped from their home. They were forced into a car separated and held in different locations.\n\nParis prosecutor Laure Beccuau stated that the kidnappers called Ledger’s leadership and demanded a large ransom in crypto. They reportedly mutilated Balland’s hand and sent a photo to Ledger to increase pressure.\n\nAround 230 police officers were mobilized after Ledger alerted authorities. David was found on January 22 in Châteauroux, 30 miles southwest of his home. Amandine was found the next day after suspect interrogations and phone tracking in Étampes 80 miles away.\n\nA small part of the ransom was paid, but it was frozen and traced, leading to nine men and one woman being arrested.\n\n🇵🇭 Bitcoin Trader's Lambo Sale Turns into Kidnapping Attempt\n\nOn January 20, Korean BTC trader Taehwa Kim met with someone in Makati, Philippines who was supposedly interested in buying his Lamborghini.\n\nAfter a test drive they stopped at a spa to \"meet a lawyer.\" Three men forced Kim into another car and tied him up.\nHe was held for three days.\n\nEventually the attackers dumped him 50km away hands still bound where he was found by police.\nWhile the attackers didn’t manage to steal his crypto, they took his car, Rolex, wallet, and apartment keys.\n\n🇪🇸 $50M Crypto Ransom Demanded from Spanish Businessman\n\nOn March 29, São Paulo police arrested a former military officer in connection with the kidnapping of a Spanish businessman.\n\nHe was approached by two men dressed in fake police uniforms, thrown into a truck, and taken to a remote location where he was held captive and asked for $50 million in crypto.\n\nLocal media said the kidnappers drugged him, but he managed to escape while one of them used the restroom.\nHe found a gas station and alerted the police, who arrested a suspect and seized a gun and ammo.\n\n🇫🇷 Kidnappers Targeted Father of Crypto Entrepreneur\n\nOn May 4, in Paris, the father of a French crypto entrepreneur was kidnapped.\nHe was taken 35 miles away to Essonne where his finger was cut off.\nThe kidnappers filmed it and sent the video to the entrepreneur, demanding €5 million in crypto.\n\nThe father was held for two days before being rescued.\nCNN reported that five suspects were arrested.\n\n🇫🇷 Daughter of Crypto Exchange Owner Escapes Abduction\n\nThe daughter and grandson of Pierre Noizat, CEO and co-founder of French crypto exchange Paymium, narrowly escaped a kidnapping attempt in Paris.\nOn May 13, three masked men tried to drag them into a van. Passersby intervened.\n\n“In central Paris, a man was grabbed by hooded figures dressed in black. They attempted a kidnapping. A passerby with a fire extinguisher scared them off” reported Le Figaro.\nThe daughter managed to disarm one attacker and a nearby crowd stepped in.\nThe attackers fled and their van was later found abandoned.\nBoth victims were hospitalized for their injuries.",
