        "text": "I want to remind you about an event that happened at the end of May\n\nA recent data breach at the cryptocurrency exchange Coinbase raised serious concerns about user safety after hackers gained access to sensitive information, including home addresses.\n\nOn May 15 Coinbase  the third-largest crypto exchange in the world  confirmed that less than 1% of its monthly users were affected by the attack which could cost the company $400 million in reimbursements\n\nHowever, the “human cost” of this data leak could be far greater for users according to Michael Arrington founder of TechCrunch and Arrington Capital\n\n“Let me be clear: this hack  involving home addresses and account balances  will lead to people dying. It likely already has” Arrington said in a May 20 post on X @arrington",
